analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers.Tests/OneDoorIntoCrossPlatformAnalyzerTests.cs:113-131:
[Fact]
public async Task ReferenceToOtherCrossPlatformType_FromBoundaries_IsNotReported()
{
    // The Boundaries gate is unchanged by the Engine type-reference extension: it stays member-access only, so a
    // type reference that calls nothing is not reported there.
    const string source = """
        using AgentGuard.CrossPlatform;

        public class Holder
        {
            private static readonly FileReader Field = null!;

            public object Typed() => typeof(FileReader);
        }
        """;

    Assert.Empty(await AnalyzerRunner.RunWithReferenceAsync<OneDoorIntoCrossPlatformAnalyzer>(
        source, "AgentGuard.Boundaries", CrossPlatformSource, "AgentGuard.CrossPlatform"));
}

analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers.Tests/OneDoorIntoPerOsAnalyzerTests.cs:124-142 is the same block with FileReader→PosixFileSystem and the trailing arguments swapped for PerOsSource/PerOsAssembly — the comment text is copied verbatim (confirmed with `grep -n 'class Holder' analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers.Tests/*.cs`, which returns exactly these two hits plus SharedAnalyzerSources.cs's own EngineHolder/EngineAbstractionsTypeReference builders — no existing builder produces this exact non-Engine-wrapped 'Holder{ Field; Typed(); }' shape). Both methods are BRAND NEW this round — `git show HEAD:analyzers/AgentGuard.Analyzers.Tests/BoundariesToCrossPlatformOneDoorAnalyzerTests.cs` and the PerOs equivalent (the files these two replace) contain no 'ReferenceToOther…' test at all — added to satisfy the new contract Acceptance 22 ('a reference to a guarded type that is not a member access, made from an AgentGuard.Boundaries compilation, is not reported by either rule'). Every other fixture shape this same round needed across AG0023/AG0029 WAS correctly extracted into a shared, parameterized SharedAnalyzerSources builder and called from both files with only the rule-specific token supplied — DerivedFrom(baseType), EngineDerivedFrom(usings, baseType), EngineHolder(usings, holderBody), EngineAbstractionsTypeReference(usings), TypeReferencePositions(guardedType), InsideContainerFactory/InsideOtherContainerMethod/InsideOtherEngineClass/InsideLambdaInContainerFactory/InsideLocalFunctionInContainerFactory(usings, expression) — so this is not a case where no pattern existed to follow; the pattern was applied to every sibling fixture in the same two files except this one. The rule-gen agent's own 'DIFF-WIDE DUPLICATION SWEEP' claims 'New fixture text introduced: none; every new string is either a moved copy … or a builder that deleted copies' — that claim is false for this pair: it is new fixture text, hand-written twice, backed by no builder.

